  "id": "frequentist-inference",
  "term": "frequentist inference",
  "definition": "Frequentist inference is the classical statistical approach used to draw conclusions from data, typically assuming that the variables being analyzed were chosen in advance rather than selected based on the same data. When variable selection is data-driven, applying this approach naively afterward can lead to biased or misleading results.",
